<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan China Steel hikes January stainless prices.</title>
<headline>Taiwan China Steel hikes January stainless prices.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's top steelmaker China Steel said on Thursday it would raise its January stainless steel prices by T$1,000 to T$36,000 per tonne.</p>
<p>The adjustment would take effect on January 1 and the company's stainless prices would be reviewed monthly, an executive said.</p>
<p>China Steel produces about 50,000 tonnes of stainless steel per year, accounting for less than 10 percent of Taiwan's annual demand, he added.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-508-0815)</p>
</text>
